WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:08.400
SCP-096 Vs SCP-272. Can the Old Iron Nail&nbsp;
finally be the thing that nails down SCP-096,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.560
the sinister, mass-murdering Shy Guy?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.560
The Nail has the ability to pin a person’s&nbsp;
shadow to the ground, potentially leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.200
them stuck there forever. If the shadow is&nbsp;
altered by changing light, it can lead to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.560
horrific bodily contortions, and attempting to&nbsp;
attack the Nail also leads to a horrific death.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.760
Because 096 only attacks people that see its&nbsp;
face, it would never attack the nail itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.920
It’s also unlikely that it would be killed&nbsp;
by a shadow-bashing due to its incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.280
durable nature. However, the truly compelling&nbsp;
question is also one we don’t have the answer to:

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.840
If 272 was pinning 096’s shadow to&nbsp;
the ground, and someone saw its face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.600
would it be pinned in place? Let us&nbsp;
know what you think in the comments.

